bio: I love those moments when the world seems to hit pause — and I just keep moving to my own rhythm.  Music is my compass, my guide, and sometimes my life raft. On the road, at home, in a loud city or on a quiet beach — I’m always with headphones on and my eyes wide open. Traveling is how I breathe deeper. New places, random conversations, the scent of streets that will never repeat themselves. I capture these moments on camera — not for the perfect shot, but to preserve the feelings that can’t be put into words.  At home, my dog waits for me — a small bundle of energy and wisdom, who reminds me better than any mentor about what matters: to move, to enjoy, to live right now.  I believe in honesty, light steps, spontaneous trips, and the most beautiful things.
